card.statement:
Let $\mathcal{C}$ be an indecomposable noncritical subset of $\mathcal{R} $. A subset of $\mathcal{C}$ of the form { $\{((k,i); (k+1,t)),\ ((k+1,s);(k,j))\}$ }with $i<j$ and $s<t$ will be called a cross.

The associated graph is as follows

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{c}
\xymatrixrowsep{0.5cm}
\xymatrixcolsep{0.1cm}\xymatrix @C=0.2em {
\scriptstyle{(k+1,s)}\ar[rrrd] & &\scriptstyle{(k+1,t)} &

&\scriptstyle{(k,i)}\ar[ru] & &\scriptstyle{(k,j)} }
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
